# Build. ANCHORED to the repo root deliberately: a bare "build/" matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently excluded the entire
# server/build source package from a commit (the ignore is why "git add" and
# "git status" both said nothing was missing). This is a single-project Gradle
# build; its output is /build only.
.gradle/
/build/
/bin/

# Generated artifacts
public/cms.js
public/cms.js.map
public/hohenheim.css
public/plumage.css
public/cms.css

# Database (plus SQLite -wal/-shm sidecars and hand-made backups)
*.db*

# Per-deployment / per-developer settings: local.dry pins the admin listener port and,
# under hohenheim.*, the public proxy ports, the TLS toggle, the roles this node runs and
# the proxy trust keys. Committing it means either a permanently dirty worktree on every
# deployment or someone's host configuration (and a SECRET) landing in git. The retired
# hohenheim.dry and the backup its adoption into local.dry leaves carry the same.
# Checked-in template: settings/local.dry.example
settings/local.dry
settings/hohenheim.dry*

# Field-encryption keyring: auto-generated on first use (also by a local test
# run), holds the keys for every .encrypted() column. Never commit it.
settings/field-encryption.keys
settings/field-encryption.keys.lock

# Git-provisioned site slots. Anchored to the repo root so a `data/` folder
# anywhere else (tests, fixtures, docs) is NOT ignored. If you reconfigure
# storage.data_path to somewhere outside the repo, add that path to
# .git/info/exclude.
/data/

# Local agent/dev-tool state
.playwright-mcp/
.swarm/

# IDE
.classpath
.project
.settings/
.factorypath
*.iml
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
public/hohenheim.css.map

# Session scratch space (agent tools); never committed.
/scratchpad/
